# Test: a read-only user is denied an edit/admin page (403)
# VALIDATES: AC-1 -- a read-only profile is gated out of the admin console and
#            config-mutation pages by RequireEditAuthz (route gate returns 403)
# PREVENTS: a read-only web user gaining edit/admin access
#
# SKIP RATIONALE: the harness seeds a single zefs local admin, so a *distinct*
# read-only web login needs config-file authz users + profile assignments, which
# the --web-only appliance the runner starts does not provision. Run this in full
# CI against an appliance that has a read-only web user configured. The
# enforcement itself is proven at the Go tier (rbac_test.go:
# TestRouteGateDeniesReadOnly, TestCanEditReflectsAuthorizer).

option=skip:reason=needs a config-file read-only web user; zefs seeds only the single local admin (see AC-6/7 runbook in the spec)
option=timeout:value=30s
option=auth:user=noc:password=ze-web-noc:role=read-only

action=login:user=noc:password=ze-web-noc
action=open:path=/admin/peer/
expect=element:text=Forbidden
